Preserve binary Secret Service values and their content type with pass.

Binary values use a versioned Base64 JSON envelope inside the GPG-encrypted
entry. UTF-8 text/plain values keep the ordinary pass representation. The
existing .properties file carries a format flag so legacy JSON passwords stay
literal. Back up .gpg and .properties files together; readers of binary entries
must use this patched provider.

Upstream issue: https://github.com/mdellweg/pass_secret_service/issues/39

